Subject: [PATCH 06994/11362] Task 11: fix induce_prompt large-grid
 scalability, ship real positive-control demo, close claimed-diff assessment
 (REQ-ARC-WMTE-5593-2)

Closes both halves ops/known-issues.md task 11 left open. Root cause,
precisely measured: _transitions_block's two full-grid renders used
to_ascii (one raw char/cell) -- exactly right by character count on lp85's
64x64 grid, but catastrophically token-inefficient (~13,400+ tokens for a
SINGLE transition's grids alone, 18,355 tokens for an 8-transition window
against a 13,824-token budget, exceed_context_size_error).

Fix, two new functions, neither modifies the existing _rle_delta (which
has its own tests + another caller):

- _rle_grid: row-wise RLE for FULL grids with an IMPLICIT run-start column
  (every cell in a row is covered, so position is the running sum of prior
  counts). An earlier attempt that spelled out an explicit column per run
  (matching _rle_delta's style) measured WORSE than to_ascii on lp85's real
  grid (short/medium runs meant per-run overhead ate the savings) --
  dropping the column fixed it: measured 2.24x/1.76x compression on the
  real INITIAL/WIN grids, lossless round-trip verified.
- _rle_delta_compact: after the full-grid fix, per-transition deltas became
  the new dominant cost (8 real deltas = 9,308 tokens). Collapses each
  changed run's NEW values as <value>x<count> instead of one value per
  cell -- measured 9,308 -> 5,992 tokens on the same 8 real deltas.

induce_prompt's own decode instructions were rewritten to match both new
formats precisely (a prompt-CONTRACT change, not just internal encoding).

Real, tokenizer-measured result (llama_cpp vocab-only against the real
Qwen3.5-9B-MTP GGUF induce_prompt targets): lp85's real 8-transition window,
18,355 -> 11,167 tokens, ~2,657 tokens of real headroom under the
13,824-token budget. Re-running experiment_5593 end-to-end (real GPU
inference, duration_s=33.452, port-8920 Qwen3.5-9B-MTP) now produces the
real positive-control demo REQ-ARC-WMTE-5593 could not: induction_ok=true,
induce_transition_count=8, goal_predicate_accuracy=0.75 (6/8 correct against
real transitions, 2 real level-ups the induced predicate missed -- an
honest induction-QUALITY finding, not a defect in the check or this fix).
Updated the stale test that asserted the old null (goal_predicate_accuracy
is None) to assert the real new result instead. results/arc_e3/lp85/
world_model.py is the real induced code from this run (lint-cleaned:
unused import removed, variables lowercased -- behavior unchanged and
re-verified after the rename).

Claimed-diff-vs-measured-diff half (Reki's pattern): re-checked every LLM
touchpoint in the pipeline (induce_prompt/refactor_prompt/CodexProposer/
LocalGGUFProposer, SGE's propose_one/reflect) for a natural-language "what
changed" self-report to hook a claimed-diff check into. Confirmed none
exists -- our LLM touchpoints write code or state a forward-looking
strategy, never a prose diff claim. Building a new self-report solely to
cross-check would cost an extra LLM call per transition, against this
gap's own corroborating evidence (forge disabled their LLM judge for cost).
Confirmed genuine dead-end in the current architecture; ops/verifier_gaps.md
updated (GAP-ARC-CLAIMED-VS-MEASURED-DIFF-5xxx stays open with the
reasoning + re-open condition documented; GAP-ARC-GOAL-HYPOTHESIS-VS-
TRANSITIONS-5xxx marked filled given the real demo above).

7 new tests (test_arc_induce_prompt_large_grid_scalability.py), all
existing tests unaffected (_rle_delta itself untouched). REQ-ARC-WMTE-5593-2
+ 2 SCENARIOs added to spec.md.

ops/known-issues.md's task 11 closure note is a separate follow-up commit:
touching that file trips the overdue-priority-lint pre-commit hook (an
unrelated, pre-existing stale priority about retro_timing_fallback wiring,
pending_count=276, exposed because research-roadmap-next.yaml is
transiently absent between the conductor's milestone .506 cycle and its
next planning pass) -- not something this task should paper over with a
fake roadmap entry or an unauthorized operator_override.

